Q: Java.util.logger new file every day A: <p>I know that this is an old post, but in a Helidon application I have combined java.util.logging and log4j v2. Helidon uses internally java.util.logging and the web access.log file is written by that framework.</p>
<p>So it appears that log4j v2 does the rolling, just by itself.</p>
<p>This shows a part of the java.util.logging property file (logging.properties):</p>
<pre><code># Configure the log handler (uses the same configuration options as FileHandler, ignores formatter)
io.helidon.webserver.accesslog.AccessLogHandler.level=INFO
io.helidon.webserver.accesslog.AccessLogHandler.pattern=access.log
io.helidon.webserver.accesslog.AccessLogHandler.append=true
# Configure the logger
io.helidon.webserver.AccessLog.level=INFO
io.helidon.webserver.AccessLog.useParentHandlers=false
io.helidon.webserver.AccessLog.handlers=io.helidon.webserver.accesslog.AccessLogHandler

</code></pre>
<p>This is an excerpt of log4j2.xml:</p>
<pre><code>...
  &lt;Appenders&gt;
    &lt;RollingFile name=&quot;access-log&quot;
                 fileName=&quot;access.log&quot;
                 filePattern=&quot;$${date:yyyy-MM}/access-%d{yyyy-MM-dd}-%i.log.gz&quot;&gt;
      &lt;PatternLayout&gt;
        &lt;Pattern&gt;%d %p %c{1.} [%t] %m%n&lt;/Pattern&gt;
      &lt;/PatternLayout&gt;
      &lt;Policies&gt;
        &lt;OnStartupTriggeringPolicy/&gt;
        &lt;TimeBasedTriggeringPolicy/&gt;
        &lt;SizeBasedTriggeringPolicy size=&quot;1 MB&quot;/&gt;
      &lt;/Policies&gt;
      &lt;DefaultRolloverStrategy&gt;
        &lt;Delete basePath=&quot;${baseDir}&quot; maxDepth=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
          &lt;IfFileName glob=&quot;access-*.log.gz&quot; /&gt;
          &lt;IfLastModified age=&quot;2d&quot; /&gt;
        &lt;/Delete&gt;
      &lt;/DefaultRolloverStrategy&gt;
    &lt;/RollingFile&gt;
  &lt;/Appenders&gt;
  &lt;Loggers&gt;
    &lt;Logger name=&quot;io.helidon.webserver.accesslog.AccessLogHandler&quot; level=&quot;debug&quot; includeLocation=&quot;false&quot; additivity=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
      &lt;AppenderRef ref=&quot;access-log&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;/Logger&gt;
  &lt;/Loggers&gt;
...
</code></pre>
